], Metz remained bedridden at his estate for a long time, under the care of [[Lady S.|a nurse]] working for the [[Huntik Foundation]]. {{source|The Vampire Loses Its Fangs}}\n\nWhen his health worsened, curtains were added to his bed frame. {{source|Ladies' Choice}}\n\nThe summoning of [[Overlos]] completely removed his curse. {{source|The Mission}}\n\n{{Clear}}","text":"Due to the curse of the Legendary Titans, Metz remained bedridden at his estate for a long time, under the care of a nurse working for the Huntik Foundation. [The Vampire Loses Its Fangs]\n\nWhen his health worsened, curtains were added to his bed frame. [Ladies' Choice]\n\nThe summoning of Overlos completely removed his curse. [The Mission]"},{"heading":"Gallery","level":2,"wikitext":"{{Gallery}}\n<gallery position=\"center\" captionalign=\"center\">\nS1E09 Dante Metz 2.png|[[Dante Vale]] in [[Metz]]' bedroom\nS1E17 Metz Lady S.jpg|Metz and [[Lady S.]]\nS1E26 Metz' country estate.png|A living room in the estate\n</gallery>","text":"S1E09 Dante Metz 2.png|Dante Vale in Metz' bedroom\nS1E17 Metz Lady S.jpg|Metz and Lady S.\nS1E26 Metz' country estate.png|A living room in the estate"},{"heading":"Trivia","level":2,"wikitext":"* The design of the house appears to be based on [https://www.historyhit.com/locations/little-moreton-hall/ Little Moreton Hall], a 16th-century half-timbered manor house located in England.\n\n[[Category:Locations]]\n[[Category:Houses]]\n[[Category:Germany]]","text":"* The design of the house appears to be based on Little Moreton Hall, a 16th-century half-timbered manor house located in England."}],"full_text":"A country estate is owned by Metz in Germany. There are no known enchantments to guard the house.\n\n==History==\nDue to the curse of the Legendary Titans, Metz remained bedridden at his estate for a long time, under the care of a nurse working for the Huntik Foundation. [The Vampire Loses Its Fangs]\n\nWhen his health worsened, curtains were added to his bed frame. [Ladies' Choice]\n\nThe summoning of Overlos completely removed his curse. [The Mission]\n\n==Gallery==\n\nS1E09 Dante Metz 2.png|Dante Vale in Metz' bedroom\nS1E17 Metz Lady S.jpg|Metz and Lady S.\nS1E26 Metz' country estate.png|A living room in the estate\n\n==Trivia==\n* The design of the house appears to be based on Little Moreton Hall, a 16th-century half-timbered manor house located in England.","raw_wikitext":"{{infobox location\n| image       = S1E17 Metz' country estate.png\n| aka         = \n| type        = House (estate)\n| location    = [[:Category:Germany|Germany]]\n| levels      = \n| areas       = \n| groups      = \n| titan       = \n| artifacts   = \n| guard titan = \n| traps       = \n| inhabitants = [[Metz]]\n| former      = [[Lady S.]]\n| first       = \"[[Absent Heroes]]\"\n| last        = \n}}A '''country estate''' is owned by [[Metz]] in Germany. There are no known enchantments to guard the house.\n\n==History==\nDue to the [[curse of the Legendary Titans]], Metz remained bedridden at his estate for a long time, under the care of [[Lady S.|a nurse]] working for the [[Huntik Foundation]]. {{source|The Vampire Loses Its Fangs}}\n\nWhen his health worsened, curtains were added to his bed frame. {{source|Ladies' Choice}}\n\nThe summoning of [[Overlos]] completely removed his curse. {{source|The Mission}}\n\n{{Clear}}\n==Gallery==\n{{Gallery}}\n<gallery position=\"center\" captionalign=\"center\">\nS1E09 Dante Metz 2.png|[[Dante Vale]] in [[Metz]]' bedroom\nS1E17 Metz Lady S.jpg|Metz and [[Lady S.]]\nS1E26 Metz' country estate.png|A living room in the estate\n</gallery>\n\n==Trivia==\n* The design of the house appears to be based on [https://www.historyhit.com/locations/little-moreton-hall/ Little Moreton Hall], a 16th-century half-timbered manor house located in England.\n\n[[Category:Locations]]\n[[Category:Houses]]\n[[Category:Germany]]","categories":["Germany","Houses","Locations"],"links":[{"target_title":"Category:Germany","label":"Germany","targe